WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.639
Why does the US have

2
00:00:01.639 --> 00:00:03.162
two big parties,

3
00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:05.236
while many European countries have

4
00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:06.269
several?

5
00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.682
Maurice Duverger observed that first-past-the-post

6
00:00:09.682 --> 00:00:11.853
voting tends to produce two

7
00:00:11.853 --> 00:00:15.398
parties. Proportional systems allow many.

8
00:00:16.078 --> 00:00:18.360
Small parties win few seats.

9
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.444
And voters avoid wasting votes

10
00:00:20.444 --> 00:00:21.577
on them.

11
00:00:21.904 --> 00:00:23.997
India uses first-past-the-post,

12
00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:25.841
yet has many parties.

13
00:00:25.841 --> 00:00:27.513
Because parties are strong in

14
00:00:27.513 --> 00:00:29.009
different states.

15
00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:30.866
Your turn.

16
00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:32.873
What does F-P-T-P tend to

17
00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:34.088
produce?
